{"role":"assistant","content":"Reproduction matches production exactly: same stderr sequence, exit 1, and `notify.sh` never invoked (the `date -v` warning is just this Linux sandbox lacking macOS date flags — harmless here). Now I'll write the fixes.\n\n**Fix 1 — `bin/nightly-review.zsh`:** rename the read-only `status` variable, merge claude's stderr into the run log so the failure reason travels with the report, and make notify failures visible locally:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_B3aI0XzEF35IKi4Wd4Kz3wP3","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"bin/nightly-review.zsh\",\"content\":\"#!/bin/zsh\\n# Nightly review of yesterday's commits, summary to Telegram.\\nset -u\\n\\nREPO=\\\"$HOME/projects/shop\\\"\\nOUT=\\\"$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md\\\"\\nNOTIFY=\\\"$HOME/bin/notify.sh\\\"\\n\\nSINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)\\nPROMPT=\\\"Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.\\nFor each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky\\n(migrations, auth, payments, deleted tests).\\nEnd with a three-line summary I can read on my phone.\\nDo not modify any file.\\\"\\n\\nnotify() {\\n  # `status` is read-only in zsh, so use $1's exit code directly; if Telegram\\n  # itself fails, at least leave a trace in stderr (launchd logs it).\\n  \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"$1\\\" || echo \\\"nightly-review: notify.sh failed (exit $?)\\\" >&2\\n}\\n\\ncd \\\"$REPO\\\" || { notify \\\"nightly review: repo missing\\\"; exit 1; }\\n\\nclaude -p \\\"$PROMPT\\\" --output-format text > \\\"$OUT\\\" 2>&1\\nrc=$?\\n\\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\\n  notify \\\"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(head -c 300 \\\"$OUT\\\")\\\"\\n  exit $rc\\nfi\\n\\nnotify \\\"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \\\"$OUT\\\")\\\"\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_9z01hqXamGqVkIGtQSf3pH9t","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"bin/notify.sh\",\"content\":\"#!/bin/bash\\n# usage: notify.sh \\\"message\\\"  — sends a Telegram message t