{"role":"assistant","content":"Found it — two stacked bugs, plus a latent third. The full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why you never heard anything**\n\n1. **The failure path crashed before it could notify.** `bin/nightly-review.zsh:19` ran `status=$?`, but `status` is a reserved read-only variable in zsh. The assignment is a fatal error, so every run died at line 19 — before the block that calls `notify.sh`. Your error log shows this exact pattern on all 6 runs (`read-only variable: status` right after claude's error), and `launchctl print` confirms 6 runs, all exit 1.\n2. **claude was never logged in under launchd.** Each run starts with `Not logged in · Please run /login` — your interactive login doesn't carry over to the launchd context, so even a working script would only have sent failure notes. Bug #1 is why you never saw them and couldn't tell.\n3. **Latent:** `notify.sh` could also die silently (`set -eu` + keychain read + `curl` without `--fail`), the same \"works by hand, not from launchd\" keychain-ACL class of problem.\n\n**Fixes (in the snapshot)**\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh` — capture the exit code in `rc`; merge claude's stderr into the run log so the Telegram failure message now contains the actual reason (e.g. `nightly review FAILED (exit 1): Not logged in · Please run /login`) instead of a Mac file path; if the report itself fails, trace it to stderr (launchd logs it) and exit non-zero.\n- `bin/notify.sh` — loud failure if the `tg-bot` keychain item is unreadable; `curl --fail` so Telegram HTTP errors surface.\n\n**Verification** — I reproduced the production failure with stubbed `claude`/notifier (script died at line 19, notifier never called), then confirmed the fixed script on all paths: claude-fails → failure note sent with the reason, exit 1; claude-succeeds → summary note, exit 0; notifier-fails → traced, exit 1. No external calls were made, per your ground rules.\n\n**One thing you must still do on the real machine:** authenticate claude for the launchd context (keychain ACL for the launchd job, or supply a token). That can't be done from this snapshot — but from now on, if it's still broken you'll get a nightly message saying exactly why."}
